WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:07.784
A ledger service reads payments and writes an entry for each into two partitions.

2
00:00:07.784 --> 00:00:11.801
Then it saves its bookmark, the next offset to read, in a third.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.935
These are three separate writes.

4
00:00:13.935 --> 00:00:17.987
Say it writes four entries, then dies before it saves the bookmark.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.748
The next instance starts from the old bookmark and writes all four again.

6
00:00:22.748 --> 00:00:24.741
Four payments are debited twice.

7
00:00:24.967 --> 00:00:30.413
A Kafka transaction makes the three writes one: all of them count, or none of them do.

8
00:00:30.633 --> 00:00:32.790
The service begins a transaction.

9
00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:36.973
Its four entries go into the partitions at once, marked as open.

10
00:00:36.973 --> 00:00:38.803
So does the new bookmark, 4.

11
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.301
On commit, the coordinator, one of the brokers, records the decision.

12
00:00:43.301 --> 00:00:48.037
Then it writes a commit marker into every partition the transaction touched.

13
00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:51.878
A marker takes an offset, but no reader ever gets it.

14
00:00:51.878 --> 00:00:57.429
A reader set to read committed gets only committed records: now pay-0 and pay-2.

15
00:00:57.633 --> 00:01:00.765
The next transaction writes pay-4 and pay-5.

16
00:01:00.765 --> 00:01:06.031
Then a plain producer, outside any transaction, appends a fee at offset 4.

17
00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:13.852
A read committed reader stops at the last stable offset, the first offset of the oldest open transaction: here, 3.

18
00:01:13.852 --> 00:01:18.416
Even the fee waits, because Kafka hands out records in offset order.

19
00:01:18.633 --> 00:01:21.525
Now a send times out, and the service aborts.

20
00:01:21.525 --> 00:01:27.564
Nothing is deleted: the coordinator writes an abort marker into the two partitions it touched.

21
00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:32.529
The last stable offset moves on, and the reader skips pay-4 to get the fee.

22
00:01:32.529 --> 00:01:36.911
A reader left on the default, read uncommitted, would take pay-4 too.

23
00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:45.896
The bookmark is still 4, so the service reads pay-4 and pay-5 again, writes them in a new transaction with bookmark 6, and commits.

24
00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:49.718
Records land in the log before the decision.

25
00:01:49.718 --> 00:01:55.443
A marker decides, and a read committed reader waits at the first record that isn't decided yet.
